// @no-instantiate
// MISCOMPILE, pinned: a NARROWED `Circle | null` handed to a generic identity `<T>(x: T): T`
// and the RESULT passed on to a `Shape` parameter. `vl check` exits 0 with no diagnostic at
// any severity and is the ONLY command that misses it — `vl build` writes the `.wasm` and
// exits 1, `vl check --codegen` exits 1, `vl run` exits 1. The engine refuses the module at
// load —
//
//   (wasmtime) type mismatch: expected (ref $type), found (ref null $type)
//
// (the two `$type`s are different heap types; the disassembler prints both by the same
// placeholder, so the message reads like a nullability complaint and is only half one.)
//
// THE NARROW DOES NOT RIDE THE PIN. Inside `if c is Circle` the checker types `c` as
// `Circle` — but the monomorphizer's argument pin reads the PARAMETER's declared annotation,
// which is still `Circle | null`, so the instance is minted `(x: Circle | null): Circle |
// null`. The value that comes back out therefore keeps the niche's `(ref null $uVarHeap[vi])`
// valtype while the checker has already typed the expression `Circle` and `area`'s parameter
// wants the union `(ref $uBox)`. Two channels answering one question about one call.
//
// PRE-EXISTING, MEASURED ON THIS EXACT FILE rather than inferred: built with the parent
// commit's compiler it is `vl check` rc 0 and `--codegen` rc 1 with
//
//   type mismatch: expected (ref $type), found i32   (at offset 0xe3)
//
// — the pin's OLD answer, `T := i32`, before it learned the variant reps. On this commit the
// same file is rc 0 / rc 1 with `expected (ref $type), found (ref null $type)` at 0xe4. Same
// cell, same silence, one rung further along: closing the pin's catch-all moved the message
// and not the outcome, which is why this is a filing and not a regression.
//
// IT IS A DIFFERENT ROOT FROM THE THREE ROWS THAT JUST CLOSED. D22 / D23 / D24 are all
// questions about a value at ONE boundary — what rep does this position want, and does the
// classifier that decides know about the niche. This one is about the boundary's TWO ENDS
// disagreeing: the pin channel and the checker channel each answer correctly for the
// question they were asked, and the answers are different types. Fixing it means deciding
// which channel owns a narrowed argument's type, which is a design question and not a
// missing arm — see `silent-class-inventory.md` D25.
//
// It is `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts`'s live specimen of the check-clean-invalid-module
// class. WHEN IT IS FIXED this file starts failing (the module instantiates), which is the
// point: delete it, graduate a `@run` row, and swap `INVALID_MODULE_SRC` for another live
// member of the class — the instruction that file has carried through eight specimens.
type Circle = { r: i32 }
type Sq = { s: i32 }
type Shape = Circle | Sq

export function area(sh: Shape) {
  if sh is Circle { return sh.r }
  return 0
}

function idg<T>(x: T): T {
  return x
}

function mkc(): Circle | null {
  return { r: 5 }
}

function go(c: Circle | null) {
  if c is Circle { return area(idg(c)) }
  return -1
}

print(go(mkc()))
